2.2.4. Gameplay Variety
● The player must use different combat strategies depending on the room layout and the types of alien enemies encountered aboard the spaceship.

 ● Early levels allow simple strategies to be effective, while later levels introduce stronger enemies and more complex room designs that require the player to adapt their approach and try new strategies.

 ● New abilities, items, and enemy behaviors are introduced gradually as the player progresses, increasing the range of possible decisions without overwhelming the player.

 ● Low-level mechanics, such as enemy behavior and basic combat actions, are handled automatically by the game, allowing the player to focus on movement, positioning, and upgrade choices.
 
2.2.5. Gameplay Consistency and Fairness
● There will be consistency in gameplay actions and outcomes, because:

 - The player will always fail by losing all health due to alien enemies or environmental hazards.
 - Enemies behave consistently based on their type, allowing players to learn patterns and plan their actions. 
- Rooms will only be cleared once all enemies have been defeated, and defeated enemies will not reappear.

● The game will be fair, as all enemies can be defeated using the player’s available weapons and abilities.

 ● Difficulty will increase gradually as the player progresses through the spaceship, through stronger enemies and more complex room layouts rather than sudden or unfair difficulty spikes.
 
 ● Story elements, including the final experimentation room and narrative reveal, will align with the gameplay mechanics already established, maintaining immersion and avoiding contradictions.
 
2.2.6. Avoiding Repetition
● The player will be able to skip cutscenes they have already seen, such as introductory or story-related sequences.

 ● The player will be able to save their progress, preventing the need to replay completed sections of the game.

 ● Repetition will be reduced through procedurally generated rooms, a variety of alien enemies, and multiple upgrades and abilities available to the player.

 ● The player will not be required to wait for actions to complete, as movement, combat, and abilities will respond immediately.


